        "text": "On Wednesday afternoons, we run a practical workshop. When we first planned it, people suggested sessions on mending clothes or fixing bicycles. In the end, though, we chose to teach people how to repair small electrical items, such as lamps. The idea is to help people keep useful things rather than throw them away. You don't need any experience, and the volunteers will check that each item is safe before you begin. Places are limited, so please contact us before turning up. We can't accept every type of electrical item, but we'll explain what you can bring when you book."
